# Git merge strategy for two-machine collaboration
# NOTE: .gitattributes only supports '#' comments. Do NOT use Markdown blockquotes.
#
# Background: two machines share one private repo. If both edit the same file,
# push is rejected (non-fast-forward) and needs manual conflict resolution.
# See reports/PM_验收看板.md section 零之四 (file ownership).

# Append-only knowledge base: both sides append at the end.
# merge=union is a git BUILT-IN driver: on conflict it keeps BOTH sides' lines
# automatically, without conflict markers. Precondition: append-only, never edit
# existing lines.
factors/FACTOR_FALSIFICATION_LOG.md merge=union

# Single-writer files (do NOT use union to avoid garbled merges):
#   reports/PM_验收看板.md        -> PM only
#   docs/*.md                     -> PM only
#   reports/R*_对齐确认表.md      -> PM creates table, implementer fills only
#                                    the "你的答案" column
# Resolve manually, owner's version wins.

# Binary / data files: never committed (see .gitignore), declared here to avoid
# accidental text merges.
*.db binary
*.parquet binary
*.xlsx binary
